<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela must compete for oil investment - Conoco.</title>
<headline>Venezuela must compete for oil investment - Conoco.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela will be the third most important region for U.S. oil giant Conoco after North America and Western Europe by 2003, the company's chief executive said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>But south-east Asia is hot on its heels in the race to attract invesments and Venezuela must continue reforms to stay competitive, Archie Dunham told journalists.</p>
<p>He was impressed with the progress made by Venezuela president Rafael Caldera, but said investors wanted more change in three key areas: VAT tax refunds, dollar tax accounting and labour laws.</p>
</text>
